  "answer": "Because it was started from the agent's shell: a process inherits its parent's whole reach. A0 plan needed 3 primitives and held 25. Narrowed with Node's permission model it holds 4 (the network still comes from the environment). The loops held the agent's reach too (R12 logged them). Only the LLM calls were at their altitude: text in, text out.",
  "fix": [
    "run A0 and A2 units under a sandbox that grants only their needs (node --permission today; a container or a Worker with no bindings tomorrow)",
    "a packet's grant becomes the sandbox's flags: the runner derives them from the packet, not from the agent",
    "the proxy's credentials reach every process in the container: a narrowed unit should run where they are not injected"
  ]
